  m_text: "multiple of a kind works in a funny way. (this does not include pip count
    of 1)\n\nfor 3 of a kind its pip count times 100 and then doubles for every extra
    dice after 3\n\nso examples are: \n4 faces with pip count 5 becomes 5 x 100 x
    2 equalling 1000\n5 faces with pip count 2 becomes 2 x 100 x 4 equalling 800\n6
    faces with pip count 6 becomes 6 x 100 x 8 eqaulling 4800\n\nthis does benifit
    with higher pip counts but to make that consistant that will cost"
